We want to package asdf along with bocl, so it's easy for users to load and use systems.

- get asdf as a git submodule
  from: https://gitlab.common-lisp.net/asdf/asdf.git
  branch: release

- Read the instructions in asdf/, build asdf,
  and install it in: $PREFIX/libexec/bocl/modules/asdf/
  (root makefile targets build  install)

- Implement REQUIRE so that:

    (require "ASDF") ; require takes a string-designator so
    (require :asdf)  ; is as good.

  loads the asdf in $PREFIX/libexec/bocl/modules/asdf/

Note REQUIRE loads a module, and usually there's a toplevel provide
form in the loaded file, which will update the *MODULES* list.

To implement loading such "system" modules, we'll need a module
definition facility:

- at boot time, bocl scans modules:

    $PREFIX/libexec/bocl/modules/*/

  and updates a BOCL:*MODULE-LIST*
  mapping module names to module files to be loaded:


BOCL::*MODULE-LIST* = ((:name "asdf" :files ("/opt/local/libexec/bocl/modules/asdf/asdf.lisp"))
                      …)

So we may define REQUIRE like:

   (defun bocl::module-name (module-plist)
       (or (get :name module-plist)
           (error 'bocl::invalid-module-plist :object module-plist :reason "Missing :NAME entry")))

   (defun bocl::module-files (module-plist)
       (or (get :files module-plist)
           (error 'bocl::invalid-module-plist :object module-plist :reason "Missing :FILES entry")))
   
   (defun REQUIRE (module-name &optional pathname-list)
     (if (null pathname-list)
        (let ((module (find (string module-name)  bocl::*module-list*
                            :key (function bocl::module-name)
                            :test (function string-equal))))
          (if module
             (require (bocl::module-name module) (bocl::module-files module))
             (error 'undefined-module-error :module-name module-name)))
        (dolist (pathname pathname-list)
           (load pathname))))

   
The way $PREFIX/libexec/bocl/modules/*/ is mapped to bocl::*module-list*
is thru the use of a module manifest file:

$PREFIX/libexec/bocl/modules/*/module.manifest
module.manifest contains:

(:name "name"
 :files ("relative/path.lisp" "relative/file.lisp"))

The module-files are merged with
$PREFIX/libexec/bocl/modules/$module-dir/ and put on
bocl::*module-list*.

Note: the directory name is not used to select the module, which
allows using different spelling or include a version
libexec/bocl/modules/asdf3/module.manifest
--> (:name "asdf" :files "asdf.lisp")

The module.manifest file must be created by the installation procedure
of bocl make install, or by a script to let the user install his own
modules.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
PROGRESS (slices 122-123, v1.3.9 / v1.3.10)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
DONE — the module system + install plumbing (everything except fetching ASDF):
- Kernel: %LIST-DIRECTORY (opendir/readdir) — sources/bocl.c.
- Boot scan (bootstrap/prelude.lisp): scans <libexec>/bocl/modules/<dir>/module.manifest,
  merges each :FILES with its module dir to absolute namestrings, and builds
  BOCL:*MODULE-LIST*.  The DIRECTORY name is not significant; the manifest :NAME
  selects the module (modules/asdf3/ can provide "ASDF").
- BOCL::MODULE-NAME / MODULE-FILES; conditions BOCL::INVALID-MODULE-PLIST and
  BOCL::UNDEFINED-MODULE-ERROR.
- REQUIRE: string-designator; with no pathnames, looks the module up by name
  (string-equal) and LOADs its files, else signals UNDEFINED-MODULE-ERROR.
    (require "ASDF")  and  (require :asdf)  both work once asdf is installed.
- make install installs every modules/<name>/ (manifest + *.lisp) into
  $PREFIX/libexec/bocl/modules/<name>/ (sources/Makefile).
- modules/README.org (conventions + ASDF plan); modules/Makefile (build/stage rule for
  ASDF, guarded on the submodule being present); top Makefile build runs make -C modules.
Verified end to end with a temporary module: installed bocl discovers it at boot and
(require :name) loads it.  No regressions (must-condition 147/0).

BLOCKED — adding ASDF itself:
- `git submodule add -b release https://gitlab.common-lisp.net/asdf/asdf.git modules/asdf-src`
  was denied automatically (fetching/executing external code needs explicit user
  authorization).  Once the user adds the submodule (command in modules/README.org),
  `make build install` builds ASDF's single-file release, stages modules/asdf/
  (asdf.lisp + manifest) and installs it, so (require :asdf) loads it.
- Open question (separate from this plumbing): whether ASDF runs unmodified on bocl's
  current CL surface — documentation.org §24 notes "It cannot run ASDF" today, so some
  CL-surface work may be needed before ASDF actually loads.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
CLOSED (v1.4.x — ASDF 3.3.7 packaged, loadable via REQUIRE)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
All deliverables of this issue are done:

- ASDF is a git submodule (modules/asdf-src, branch release, ASDF 3.3.7).
- modules/Makefile builds the single-file release (cat of the UIOP+ASDF sources)
  and stages modules/asdf/ (asdf.lisp + module.manifest); a bocl UIOP port
  (modules/asdf-bocl-port.patch) is applied to the sources during the build.
- make install installs modules/asdf/ into $PREFIX/libexec/bocl/modules/asdf/.
- The module system (BOCL:*MODULE-LIST*, %SCAN-MODULES over <libexec>/bocl/
  modules/<dir>/module.manifest, BOCL::MODULE-NAME/MODULE-FILES, the
  INVALID-MODULE-PLIST / UNDEFINED-MODULE-ERROR conditions) and the enhanced
  REQUIRE (string designator; module-name lookup; PROVIDE/*MODULES* tracking)
  are implemented in bootstrap/prelude.lisp.
- ASDF 3.3.7 now fully LOADS and RUNS on bocl — this took a chain of general
  CL/CLOS conformance fixes (see uiop-bocl-porting.issue): O(1) DO-SYMBOLS,
  destructuring macro lambda-lists, structured pathnames, DEFGENERIC/DEFMETHOD
  (setf name), (setf documentation), CLHS-7.5.3 slot merging, CLOS-aware
  SUBTYPEP/TYPEP over class objects, computed DEFCLASS :initforms, and
  :allocation :class slots — resolving the "Open question: whether ASDF runs
  unmodified on bocl" (it runs, via the #+bocl UIOP port).

Verified end to end: %SCAN-MODULES discovers the asdf manifest and builds the
(:NAME "asdf" :FILES (".../asdf.lisp")) plist; (require :asdf) then loads it,
(asdf:asdf-version) => "3.3.7", *MODULES* gains "ASDF", and a second
(require "ASDF") is a no-op.

REMAINING ASDF work (tracked separately, NOT part of this packaging issue):
using ASDF to DEFSYSTEM + OPERATE on real systems — see uiop-bocl-porting.issue.
